After buying vegetables, I go to the nearby butcher shop.
It is very busy there on Sunday morning.
Even so, there is enough chicken in the shop.
I ask the shopkeeper for chicken.
"Brother, I want half a kilo of chicken," I say.
He takes half a kilo of meat.
"Is this for making curry?" he asks me.
"Yes, it is for making curry," I reply.
I tell him, "First, this must be cleaned well."
"After that, it must be cut into small pieces for the curry."
Small pieces are always good for curry.
He nods his head.
He quickly chops the meat and makes it into small pieces.
Then he puts it in a packet and gives it to me.
I give him one hundred and sixty rupees.
I put the chicken in my bag.
It is still raining heavily outside.
I open the umbrella and walk home quickly.
Now I must start making the curry.
